                                        "sense_id": "893677a7-fe98-3a97-bf38-01c807386a1a",
                                        "entry_id": "3fe752ea-7fc9-3510-9c34-beb9b49a5e66",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Capable of being thrown."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e24f71ac-8e30-3ec3-9a7b-d074d597dda2",
                                        "entry_id": "3fe752ea-7fc9-3510-9c34-beb9b49a5e66",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Capable of being thrown in the manner of an exception."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c35841c4-cf6f-42a8-84e5-04e8a0078952",
                                                "sense_id": "e24f71ac-8e30-3ec3-9a7b-d074d597dda2",
                                                "text": "For an object to be throwable, it must be directly or indirectly derived from the Throwable class."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d3172f8-d540-4191-8f43-7a2b8fba440c",
                                                "sense_id": "e24f71ac-8e30-3ec3-9a7b-d074d597dda2",
                                                "text": "In general, each function may specify a list of throwable objects […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "286ff169-de40-45d4-8263-2bf24256f7ff",
                                                "sense_id": "e24f71ac-8e30-3ec3-9a7b-d074d597dda2",
                                                "text": "[…] if you need to make certain symbols visible externally for debugging purposes or for catching exceptions for throwable entities within a library."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "throwable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2d169c3-a65b-38c9-925f-2f0173ccbab8",
                                        "entry_id": "e06ebf40-b03d-3892-9432-8be6cd63119a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that is throwable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17d97b6c-a7dd-43aa-bbf5-d8a8455f3b90",
                                                "sense_id": "e2d169c3-a65b-38c9-925f-2f0173ccbab8",
                                                "text": "Speaking of cycling, most things are recycled: There are bins for paper and bins for cans. Most plastic throwables are simply not allowed (though organizers haven’t quite found a substitute for forks, spoons and knives)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65737cec-853d-4bda-94ea-d18c2d826b54",
                                                "sense_id": "e2d169c3-a65b-38c9-925f-2f0173ccbab8",
                                                "text": "Transforming objects’ states identically by manipulating them in the same way affords infants a way to begin constructing functional equivalence classes even when the objects do not belong to the same predicate class (Piaget, 1952a). For example, simultaneously throwing a doll and a cup transforms both into functionally equivalent ‘throwables.’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbd4e675-c85c-4963-a0fe-f18cf33bce46",
                                                "sense_id": "e2d169c3-a65b-38c9-925f-2f0173ccbab8",
                                                "text": "Aside from chucking things, you can also dash – useful for stealing throwables right out of the opposition’s meaty hands or even catching objects mid-air as they sail right at you."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aee7772f-6d30-3778-b1f3-79c1db793b6a",
                                        "entry_id": "e06ebf40-b03d-3892-9432-8be6cd63119a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any object that can be thrown in the manner of an exception."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80e55375-ef40-4441-8631-7658b180cb2a",
                                                "sense_id": "aee7772f-6d30-3778-b1f3-79c1db793b6a",
                                                "text": "Exceptions are thrown when some module of the project detects an error condition or if it handles some standard Java throwables."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
